  "description": "Family F, centralindia. Replication lag against REAL network round-trip time: the subscriber is a physically separate machine in the centralindia Azure region, so the 207.0 ms is genuine inter-region latency, not emulation. Nothing is injected and nothing needs calibrating. The offered load is 6 MB/s, identical in every region. That it sits far below saturation is established per region by preflight_region.py, which measures this subscriber's sustained apply throughput before the campaign and requires at least four times the offered load - see the hardware block. RTT is the only quantity that differs between the points of this dose-response.",
